Web Audio, rendered in the engine and played by the host page.

The engine renders render quanta on a thread of its own into a ring of planar
float samples in its shared memory; an AudioWorklet in the host page reads the
ring and plays it, at the context's sample rate (the host resamples to the
device). With an AudioWorklet in the page, quanta render on the worklet's
thread. WAVE files, WebKit's HRTF database among them, decode in the engine;
compressed audio decodes in the host browser and comes back as planar samples.
The FFT is a radix-2 transform of the port's own.

